import FourColor.CfQuiz
import FourColor.Configurations

/-!
# The quizzes of the reducible configurations, precomputed

Generated by a Lean computation from `FourColor/Configurations.lean`; do not
edit by hand.

Evaluating `cfquiz` on the 633 configurations is far beyond what the Lean
kernel can do in the memory of an ordinary machine, but the presentation
scripts need the resulting quiz tree in a form the kernel can read off.  So the
quizzes are stored here as a literal, `theQuizzes`, and proved equal to what
`cfquiz` computes in blocks of at most 5 configurations — each block is one
`decide +kernel` check, small enough to run on its own.  `theQuizzes_eq`
assembles the blocks into the statement the rest of the development uses.

## Main definitions

* `theQuizzes` — the quiz and symmetry flag of each configuration of
  `theConfigs`.

## Main results

* `theQuizzes_eq` — `theQuizzes` is what `cfquiz` computes on `theConfigs`.
-/

namespace FourColor

set_option maxRecDepth 100000

